      "text_raw": "The simplest transconduc-\ntor is evidently a differential\npair. Its Gm is simply the\ntransconductance of the\nMOSTs.\nIts distortion is quite\nhigh, however. Its IM\n3\nis proportional to the rela-\ntive current swing squared.\nIt can be reduced for\nlarge values of V −V .\nGS T\nExceedingly high values\nare required, however, to\nachieve low distortion for a\n1 V input signal amplitude.\nAdditional feedback or\nother tricks will therefore be\nrequired to remedy this.",
